{% comment %}
  Shared card anatomy for every "work" listing on the site (home selected
  work, research, policy writing, media): mono eyebrow -> serif title ->
  sans finding line -> optional mono metadata row. Left border 3px in the
  category color (teal = academic/peer-reviewed, amber = policy/media).

  The container is a <div>, not an <a>, because the metadata row is allowed
  to hold its own links (PDF / code / BibTeX) — nesting an <a> inside an <a>
  is invalid HTML, so the title itself carries the primary link instead.

  Params:
    url      - required. Title links here.
    category - "academic" (teal) or "policy" (amber).
    eyebrow  - mono eyebrow text, e.g. "PEER-REVIEWED · 2024".
    title    - serif technical title (plain text or markdown-safe HTML).
    finding  - sans plain-language finding line.
    meta     - optional raw HTML for the metadata row (venue, coauthors,
               PDF/code/BibTeX links). May contain its own <a> tags.
    external - optional. Set true if `url` leaves the site (adds
               rel="noopener noreferrer" and target="_blank").

  Usage:
    {% include work-card.liquid url=paper.url category="academic"
       eyebrow="PEER-REVIEWED · 2024" title=paper.title finding=paper.finding %}
{% endcomment %}
<div class="work-card work-card--{{ include.category }}">
  <span class="work-card__eyebrow">{{ include.eyebrow }}</span>
  <h3 class="work-card__title">
    <a
      href="{{ include.url }}"
      {% if include.external %}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      {% endif %}
    >
      {{- include.title -}}
    </a>
  </h3>
  <p class="work-card__finding">{{ include.finding }}</p>
  {% if include.meta %}
    <div class="work-card__meta">{{ include.meta }}</div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
